  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Katti. See rules.objective and rules.gameplay for details.',
    Player: "Katti (meaning 'cut' or 'bundle' in some dialects) is a traditional Indian banking and gambling game of pure chance, closely related to Andar Bahar. Originating in South India (Karnataka and Tamil Nadu), the game involves betting on which of two piles ('Andar'/Inside or 'Bahar'/Outside) will first receive a card matching the rank of a central 'House' card. It is a staple of festival gambling and modern online casinos.",
    objective: 'Predict which of the two piles (Andar or Bahar) will be dealt a card that matches the rank of the House card.',
    gameplay: '1. The dealer deals one card face-up in the center (The **House Card**).\n2. Players place bets on either Andar or Bahar.\n3. **The First Deal Rule**: If the House card is **Black** (Clubs/Spades), the first card is dealt to Andar. If it is **Red** (Hearts/Diamonds), it is dealt to Bahar.\n4. The dealer continues dealing cards alternately to Andar and Bahar until a card of the same rank as the House card appears.',
    keyRules: [
      'First card goes to Andar if House card is black (Clubs/Spades), to Bahar if red (Hearts/Diamonds).',
      'Dealer deals alternately to Andar and Bahar until a card matches the House card rank.',
      'Bets pay on the pile that receives the matching card first.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
